# Git (minimal)

Authoritative detail: `docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md`.

## Lanes

- `main` — clean, meaningful commits only; do not start product edits on `main`
- `work/<task>` — local WIP sandbox; any commit messages OK; **never push** `work/*`
- `review/<task>` — cleaned 1–3 logical commits for transfer to `main`

## Always

- Commit / push / merge / tag **only** when the user explicitly asks
- Never delete unrelated personal untracked files or folders
- Never run destructive cleanup just to get a “clean tree”
- Never rewrite pushed `main` history
- Never move or rewrite existing preplay tags

## Before source changes

If on `main` and the task changes source/config → create/switch to `work/<task>` first.

Do not hardcode current branch or HEAD — check at task time.
